 (1D) Array",definition:"A fixed-length collection of values of the same type accessed by one index; Python lists can be used as an equivalent but can change length",example:'Python: names = ["Ali", "Ben", "Cara"]; names[0] is "Ali". Valid indices are 0 to len(names) - 1'},{term:"Two-Dimensional (2D) Array",definition:"A table-like collection accessed by row and column indices; Python can represent it as a list of lists",example:"With zero-based indexing, grid[2][3] accesses the third row and fourth column; pass grid to a function as an argument to process its rows"},{term:"Structured Query Language (SQL)",definition:"A language used to search for and retrieve data from a database",example:"SELECT name FROM students WHERE grade = 9;"},{term:"SQL SELECT",definition:"Retrieves specific fields from a database table, with optional conditions",example:"SELECT name, score FROM results WHERE score > 50;"},{term:"SQL FROM",definition:"Specifies which database table the SELECT statement should retrieve data from",example:"SELECT name FROM students; pulls the name column from the students table"},{term:"SQL WHERE",definition:"Filters the rows returned by a SELECT statement so only rows that match a condition are included",example:"SELECT name FROM students WHERE year = 11; returns only Year 11 students"},{term:"Sub Program",definition:"A named block of code that performs a specific task, called from the main program to reduce repetition",example:"Using a sub program called calculateAverage() whenever you need to find a mean"},{term:"Function",definition:"A subprogram that returns a value to its caller and may receive parameters",example:"Python: def first(items): return items[0] accepts an array/list; def copy(items): return items[:] returns a new list"},{term:"Procedure",definition:"A subprogram that performs a task without returning a useful value; it may receive parameters",example:'Python: def printWelcome(): print("Welcome") needs no parameters; printWelcome() calls it. 